        { "$comment": "P69 (lane cs): `__declspec(allocate(\"name\"))` places an object in a NAMED SECTION (with `#pragma section`, cl's idiom for registering an initializer in `.CRT$XCU`). MEASURED on cl 19.51: the initializer so registered RUNS before main. This compiler has no source-level section placement, so the object would land in an ordinary data section and the registration would silently not happen: refused by name.", "names": ["__declspec(allocate_)"], "effect": "unsupported", "reason": "it places the object in a named section, and this compiler has no source-level section placement" }
